**III.7** **make use of, avail oneself of,** τῆς τύχης{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Iphigenia Aulidensis” 56.}}
**III.8** Geometry texts, of bodies and surfaces, **to be in contact,** {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Physica” 231a22, compare “Metaphorical” 1002a34, +others, 2nd c.AD: Sextus Empiricus Philosophus “adversus Mathematicos” 3.35}}; of lines or curves, **meet,** {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|3rd c.BC: Euclides Geometra 3 “Def.” 2}}; **touch,** {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|[prev. author] 4 “Def.” 5, 3rd c.BC: Archimedes Geometra “περὶ σφαίρας καὶ κυλίνδρου” 1.28}}; **pass through** a point, {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|3rd c.BC: Euclides Geometra 4 “Defs.” 2,6}}; of points, **lie on** a line or curve,{{Refs|[prev. work] “Defs.” 1,3}}; ἅπτεται τὸ σημεῖον θέσει δεδομένης εὐθείας **the locus** of the point **is** a given straight line, {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|[prev. author] cited in 3rd c.AD(?): Pappus Mathematicus 656.6, +others}}
**B** _active_, **kindle, set on fire** (i.e. by **contact** of fire), {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 8.52, etc.}} (so in _middle_, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|3rd c.BC: Callimachus Epicus “Hymnus in Dianam” 116); ἐρείκης θωμὸν ἅψαντες πυρί 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 295: _metaphorically_, πυρσὸν ὕμνων 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “I.” 4(3).43}}:—_passive_, **to be set on fire,** ὁ μοχλὸς ἐλάϊνος ἐν πυρὶ μέλλεν ἅψεσθαι{{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 9.379}}; ὡς ἅφθη τάχιστα τὸ λήιον.. ἅψατο νηοῦ as soon as the corn **caught fire,** it **set fire to** the temple, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.19}}; πυρῆς ἤδη ἁμμένης{{Refs 5th c.BC+|[prev. work] 86; ἧπται πυρί 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Helena” 107.}}
**B.II** ἅ. πῦρ **kindle** a fire, {{Refs|[prev. work] 503}}:—_passive_, ἄνθρακες ἡμμένοι **red-hot** embers, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 4.100; δᾷδ᾽ ἐνεγκάτω τις ἡμμένην 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nubes” 1490, compare “Pl.” 301.}}
